Subject: [PATCH] Let strongly consistent presence checks ask about hits too

Base: facebook/buck2 9a1876786f32806f6b65fc51f4c1c3077efc38a5 plus the
preceding Sekka patches.

A digest that remembers an expiration beyond the headroom is answered
without an RPC. Meta's CAS honours those expirations; NativeLink evicts by
LRU at any time. A cache upload then trusted a remembered expiration,
skipped re-uploading an evicted output and wrote an action result naming
it, which NativeLink's completeness check hides: the entry was lost.

NegativeCache::Bypassed already means a strongly consistent read decides
misses. It now decides hits as well. Its callers are cache uploads, CAS
artifact downloads and the TTL refresher, which asks about near-expiry
digests anyway. Allowed checks, used for execution inputs, are unchanged.

diff --git a/app/buck2_execute/src/re/presence.rs b/app/buck2_execute/src/re/presence.rs
index 508b0c8..205d4cc 100644
--- a/app/buck2_execute/src/re/presence.rs
+++ b/app/buck2_execute/src/re/presence.rs
@@ -45,7 +45,9 @@ pub enum NegativeCache {
     /// miss, which then merely do redundant work.
     Allowed,
     /// A strongly consistent read decides before a miss is reported. Required when a miss is an
-    /// error, or is recorded as the blob's expiration.
+    /// error, or is recorded as the blob's expiration. The CAS also decides every hit: an
+    /// expiration the digest remembers is not a lease when the CAS evicts by LRU, and a cache
+    /// upload that trusts one writes an action result naming a blob that is already gone.
     Bypassed,
 }
 
@@ -169,8 +171,9 @@ impl CasPresence {
     }
 
     /// One answer per digest, in order. A digest that already knows an expiration beyond
